# Dockerfile Standards

## Required in every Dockerfile
- Multi-stage build (minimum: build stage + runtime stage)
- Non-root user: `USER 1001` (or named user)
- `HEALTHCHECK` instruction
- Pinned image versions — never `:latest`
- Copy dependency manifests **before** source code (layer caching)
- Alpine or slim base images

## .NET Pattern
```dockerfile
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:8.0 AS build
WORKDIR /src
COPY *.csproj .
RUN dotnet restore
COPY . .
RUN dotnet publish -c Release -o /app/publish

FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:8.0 AS runtime
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=build /app/publish .
USER 1001
EXPOSE 8080
HEALTHCHECK CMD wget --no-verbose --tries=1 --spider http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1
ENTRYPOINT ["dotnet", "YourApp.dll"]
```

## Next.js Pattern
```dockerfile
FROM node:20-alpine AS deps
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json package-lock.json ./
RUN npm ci

FROM node:20-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY . .
RUN npm run build

FROM node:20-alpine AS runner
WORKDIR /app
ENV NODE_ENV=production
COPY --from=builder /app/.next/standalone ./
COPY --from=builder /app/.next/static ./.next/static
USER 1001
EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["node", "server.js"]
```

## Common Mistakes
- ❌ `COPY . .` before installing dependencies → breaks layer cache
- ❌ Running as root in production
- ❌ Missing `.dockerignore` → sends `node_modules`/`bin`/`obj` to daemon
- ❌ `:latest` tags → non-reproducible builds
